ange exactly one property at a time: (a) demote the node kept with the leader from voter to non-voter through DemoteVoter, (b) keep it a voter, (c) keep it a non-voter but cut the leader from everyone. The prediction is success in (a) and non-success in (b) and (c); the same outcome in (b) or (c) would refute the suffrage-attribution explanation.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s_verify_leader\",\n        \"s_verify_branch\",\n        \"s_quorum_size\",\n        \"s_repl_state\",\n        \"s_notify_all\",\n        \"s_heartbeat_notify\",\n        \"s_update_last_appended\",\n        \"s_verify_vote\",\n        \"s_suffrage_doc\",\n        \"s_verify_doc\",\n        \"s_commitment_voters\"\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence\": [],\n      \"limitations\": [],\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"knowledge\": [],\n      \"open_gaps\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"101498ecfbb945e0b48676dd9e9f4172-gap-0\",\n          \"question\": \"Does the false confirmation extend past the leader's own lease window, i.e. does VerifyLeader report success while a different node already holds leadership and has committed a write that the partitioned leader's FSM lacks? The window is bounded because ValidateConfig requires LeaderLeaseTimeout <= HeartbeatTimeout and checkLeaderLease counts only voters, so the partitioned leader steps down within about one lease interval; a successor harness with per-node timing (long leader lease, short follower election timers) is needed to place a voter-majority election inside that window.\",\n          \"experiment_id\": null,\n          \"operation_id\": \"101498ecfbb945e0b48676dd9e9f4172\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"latest_execution\": {\n        \"id\": \"df528a8a25a04cbd9fb1cc12319f3467\",\n        \"experiment_id\": \"101498ecfbb945e0b48676dd9e9f4172-experiment\",\n        \"status\": \"completed\",\n        \"exit_code\": 0,\n        \"record\": \"logs/df528a8a25a04cbd9fb1cc12319f3467/check.json\",\n        \"observations\": \"logs/df528a8a25a04cbd9fb1cc12319f3467/observations.json\"\n      },\n      \"latest_interpretation\": null,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n        \"id\": \"101498ecfbb945e0b48676dd9e9f4172-question-0\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"101498ecfbb945e0b48676dd9e9f4172-knowledge-0\",\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"On a leader, verifyLeader() registers the pending verifyFuture on every entry of leaderState.replState and compares accumulated votes against a quorum size computed only from voters; every followerReplication whose AppendEntries/heartbeat response reports success calls notifyAll(true), which increments verifyFuture.votes without consulting the peer's ServerSuffrage. Therefore a peer recorded as Nonvoter (or Staging) contributes a vote to the VerifyLeader confirmation.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"Leader state; the peer is present in r.configurations.latest.Servers with Suffrage != Voter and is reachable by the leader's transport; the verifyFuture is still pending (notifyCh != nil) when the response arrives.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s_verify_leader\",\n        \"s_verify_branch\",\n        \"s_quorum_size\",\n        \"s_repl_state\",\n        \"s_notify_all\",\n        \"s_heartbeat_notify\",\n        \"s_update_last_appended\",\n        \"s_verify_vote\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {},\n      \"knowledge\": [],\n      \"operation_id\": \"101498ecfbb945e0b48676dd9e9f4172\",\n      \"uses\": [],\n      \"use_paths\": {},\n      \"last_correction\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"experiments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"101498ecfbb945e0b48676dd9e9f4172-experiment\",\n      \"investigation_id\": \"101498ecfbb945e0b48676dd9e9f4172-question-0\",\n      \"previous_id\": null,\n      \"basis\": \"fixed-experiments/101498ecfbb945e0b48676dd9